WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.029
Host: Explain why rapid shallow breaths can be
less efficient than slower deeper breaths at
the

2
00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:08.468
Host: same minute ventilation.

3
00:00:08.468 --> 00:00:16.521
Guide: A fixed conducting-airway volume takes
up more of each small breath. After
subtracting dead space,

4
00:00:16.521 --> 00:00:24.244
Guide: less fresh air reaches gas-exchanging
alveoli each minute, even when total minute
ventilation is unchanged.

5
00:00:24.244 --> 00:00:31.208
Host: At the same 6 L/min minute ventilation
and a fixed 150 mL dead space,

6
00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:34.921
Host: which pattern gives greater alveolar
ventilation?

7
00:00:34.921 --> 00:00:47.504
Guide: 500 mL at 12 breaths/min. This gives
(500−150)×12 = 4.2 L/min,

8
00:00:47.504 --> 00:00:52.063
Guide: because less of total ventilation is
wasted in dead space.
